  "worked_solution": "**Method 1**\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\nThe resulting graph is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255908/assets/46e0576ed289d58602744ab64f253f7014cf6ce7ddc501ed503aadde6eb9a0d3.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the maximum value is $y=\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe know that that $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ has a maximum value of $1.$ \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\le 1\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the above inequality by $\\frac{5}{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x & \\le \\frac{5}{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & \\le \\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the maximum value of $\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is $\\frac{5}{2}.$",
